# Keep the production image build context small and, more importantly,
# keep the Docker CLI from ever trying to read supabase/volumes — its
# volumes/db/data directory is bind-mounted Postgres data owned by the
# container's postgres uid, unreadable by the host user, and large. The
# app image doesn't need anything under supabase/ to build or run (it only
# talks to Supabase over the network at request time), so exclude the
# whole directory rather than relying on a build-time workaround.
supabase/

# Dependencies / build output — reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
.next
.git
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions
coverage

# Env files — every credential is supplied at `docker build --build-arg`
# (the two NEXT_PUBLIC_* values, inlined at build time) or `docker run -e`/
# Compose `environment:` (everything else) time. Never bake a real .env
# into the image.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Misc
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.md
!README.md
